# This project is built and executed exclusively on Linux (Docker images and
# Singularity on HPC), so the working tree is LF on every platform, not just
# in the index.
#
# This is not a style preference. `source_contract_fingerprint` and
# `search_runtime_fingerprint` hash the *bytes* of the Python sources, and
# `docker build` COPYs the working tree. A CRLF checkout on Windows would
# produce an image whose fingerprints differ from the repository, silently
# failing the verified search migration in src/nianetvae/search/migration.py.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated / binary artifacts must never be transformed.
*.csv    -text
*.joblib binary
*.sif    binary
*.png    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.dill   binary
*.zip    binary
